@corporategoth I think you're on to something with the throttling / cooldown 👍

I'd suggest to explore wrapping `homeassistant.components.mqtt.async_subscribe` with a `homeassistant.helpers.debounce.Debouncer`, with the `immediate` flag set to `False`. The debounce time can probably be relatively short, maybe 100 ms or so to get ride of the unwanted startup behavior where all entities race to setup their subscriptions.

Obviously the function `homeassistant.components.mqtt.async_subscribe` itself can't be wrapped with a Debouncer, the goal is to debounce calls to `paho.mqtt.Client.subscribe`.

